                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>NO, enteric coatings are placed on a medication to make sure it is not exposed to the stomach or its acids. Once dissolved in the small intestines, it goes straight to the liver to experience the hepatic first pass.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "tip": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>Indeed,&nbsp;enteric coatings are placed on a medication to make sure it is not exposed to the stomach or its acids. Once dissolved in the small intestines, it goes straight to the liver to experience the hepatic first pass.&nbsp;</div>\n"
